// frame.data foundation — v2.1.3+ capability contract for Database operations.
//
// The `can Persist:` declaration is what Database.save/delete/etc. use to
// verify at compile time that an entity supports persistence. Every entity
// that wants to be persisted declares `class E can Persist` and implements
// the two methods below by forwarding to its paired data class:
//
//     class User can Persist
//         UserData data
//         string email
//
//         functions:
//             boolean save()
//                 return UserData.save(this)
//             boolean delete()
//                 return UserData.delete(this)
//
// See spec DAT-S000 for the full contract.
//
// This file exists because the current typed-emission bridge surface has no
// capability-emission bridge — the plugin cannot emit `can` declarations
// itself. When the compiler adds `_emit_capability` (tracked as team-prompt
// task #1300), the plugin will emit `can Persist:` from its module_helpers
// slot and you can delete this file safely.

can Persist:
	boolean save()
	boolean delete()
